{"Title":"Order relative to authorizing the joint committee on Mental Health, Substance Use and Recovery to make an investigation and study of a certain current Senate documents relative to harm reduction and racial justice.","BillNumber":"S2787","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"J18","Name":"Joint Committee on Mental Health, Substance Use and Recovery","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J18","ResponseDate":"2024-05-15T16:31:02.697"},"Cosponsors":[],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2787/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Order","Pinslip":"Senate, May 20, 2024 -- The committee on Mental Health, Substance Use and Recovery, to whom was referred the petitions (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1243) of Julian Cyr, Liz Miranda, Vanna Howard and Lindsay N. Sabadosa for legislation relative to harm reduction and racial justice, report the accompanying Order  (Senate, No. 2787).","DocumentText":"\tOrdered, That the committee on Mental Health, Substance Use and Recovery be authorized and directed to make an investigation and study of certain current Senate document numbered 1243 relative to harm reduction and racial justice.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Study","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J18","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J18"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Discharge to Another Committee","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J40","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J40"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}